,9,11,12,15,16,17,20,22,23,24,25,26,27,30,32,33]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[5,30,33]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[20,32]},{"id":"amoz_240","name":"Amoz","also":"","summary":"Strong, the father of the prophet Isaiah (2 Kings 19:2, 20; 20:1; Isa. 1:1; 2:1). As to his personal history little is positively known.","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20,32]},{"id":"manasseh_1930","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":24,"father":"Hezekiah","mother":"Hephzi-bah","v":[33]}],"places":[{"id":"assyria_111","name":"Assyria","kind":"Region","lat":36.50969,"lon":43.2282,"summary":"The name derived from the city Asshur on the Tigris, the original capital of the country, was originally a colony from Babylonia, and was ruled by viceroys from that kingdom.","verses":116,"v":[1,4,7,9,10,11,21,22]},{"id":"millo_802","name":"Millo","kind":"","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"Probably the Canaanite name of some fortification, consisting of walls filled in with earth and stones, which protected Jerusalem on the north as its outermost defence.","verses":6,"v":[5]},{"id":"lachish_711","name":"Lachish","kind":"City","lat":31.56522,"lon":34.84907,"summary":"Impregnable, a royal Canaanitish city in the Shephelah, or maritime plain of Palestine (Josh. 10:3, 5; 12:11). It was taken and destroyed by the Israelites (Josh. 10:31-33).","verses":22,"v":[9]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[19,22,23,25,26,33]},{"id":"gihon_473","name":"Gihon","kind":"","lat":31.77312,"lon":35.23719,"summary":"The only natural spring of water in or near Jerusalem is the “Fountain of the Virgin”, which rises outside the city walls on the west bank of the Kidron valley.","verses":5,"v":[30]},{"id":"babylon_151","name":"Babylon","kind":"City","lat":32.53617,"lon":44.42082,"summary":"The Greek form of BABEL; Semitic form Babilu, meaning “The Gate of God.” In the Assyrian tablets it means “The city of the dispersion of the tribes.”","verses":255,"v":[31]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[310,428,428,1697,571,571,5576,4428,804,804,935,935,935,3063,2583,2583,2583,5921,1219,1219,5892,559,1234,1234,1234,413,413],[2396,2396,7200,3588,5576,935,935,4421,4421,4421,5921,3389],[3289,3289,5973,8269,8269,1368,1368,1368,5640,5640,5640,4325,4325,5869,5869,5869,2351,5892,5892,5826,5826,5826,5826,5826,5826,5826],[7227,5971,6908,5640,5640,3605,3605,4599,4599,5158,5158,5158,7857,7857,8432,776,776,4100,4428,4428,4428,804,804,935,4672,4672,7227,4325,4325,559,559],[2388,2388,2388,2388,1129,1129,3605,6555,6555,6555,6555,2346,2346,5927,5927,5927,5927,4026,4026,4026,312,312,312,312,2351,2346,2388,2388,4407,4407,4407,5892,5892,5892,1732,1732,6213,6213,6213,7230,7230,7230,7973,4043,4043],[5414,5414,4421,8269,5921,5971,5971,6908,6908,413,413,413,7339,7339,5892,5892,5892,8179,1696,1696,1696,3824,559],[2388,2388,553,553,408,408,3372,3372,2865,2865,6440,4428,4428,804,804,6440,1995,1995,1995,5973,5973,3588,7227,7227,7227,7227,7227,5973,5973,5973,5973,5973],[5973,5973,5973,5973,2220,222